    "path": "data/beverage_temperature_series.csv"
  }
}
```

Now I need to examine the data more carefully. I notice there's a jump at time 80 minutes (from 49.088 to 54.239) and another at time 121 minutes (from 46.75 to 39.828). This suggests there might be some intervention or measurement anomaly. Let me create a Python script to visualize the data and understand it better.

First, let me check if Python is available and install necessary packages.

```json
{
  "tool": "run_shell",
  "args": {
    "cmd": "python --version"
  }
}
```

Good. Now let me create a directory structure and write a Python script to analyze the data.

```json
{
  "tool": "run_shell",
  "args": {
    "cmd": "mkdir -p code outputs report/images"
  }
}
```

Let me use Windows-compatible commands.

